>> title: Phở Broth
>> category: Soups
>> tags: beef, vietnamese, stock, star anise, stovetop
>> counters: Phở & Bánh Mì
>> aka: pho broth, nước dùng phở, nuoc dung pho, pho stock, beef pho broth, phở bò broth, pho base, the broth for pho
>> pairs-with: pho-bo
>> servings: 8
>> time: 6 hr 30 min
>> step.1: parboil 10 min, rinse every bone
>> step.2: char over a flame 10 min
>> step.3: toast 3 min, tie the sachet
>> step.4: simmer 6 hr, skimming
>> step.5: season and strain

Cover @beef marrow bones{4%lb}(1.8 kg) and @oxtail{2%lb}(900 g) with @cold water{}(to cover) in a #stockpot{}, bring to a hard boil and ~parboil{10%min}, then tip the lot into the sink, rinse every bone under the tap and scrub the pot. Skipping this is what makes grey, muddy broth, and there is no skimming your way back from it.

Char @yellow onions{2%large}(halved) and @fresh ginger{4%in}(halved lengthways) directly on a burner or under a broiler ~char{10%min}, turning until blackened in patches, then scrape the loose ash away.

Toast @star anise{5%whole}, @cinnamon stick{1}, @whole cloves{4}, @coriander seed{1%Tbs} and @black cardamom{1%pod}(cracked) in a dry #skillet{} ~toast{3%min}, until they smell like the shop, then tie them into a #spice sachet{}.

Simmer @&(~3)parboiled bones{}, @&(~2)charred aromatics{} and @&(~1)spice sachet{} with @beef brisket{2%lb}(900 g) and @water{6%qt}(5.7 L) at a bare tremble ~simmer{6%hr}, skimming hard for the first hour and never letting it boil. Lift the brisket out at ninety minutes, when a skewer slides in clean, and chill it — that is the sliced meat in the bowl. Pull the sachet at ninety minutes too, or the star anise takes the whole pot over.

Season @&(~1)broth{} with @fish sauce{1/3%cup}(80 mL), @rock sugar{1%oz}(30 g) and @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, then strain it through a fine sieve. It should taste a shade too strong on its own; the noodles and the raw beef in the bowl bring it back down.
